# Pairs with NoStrandedPrepare. The compensation fan-out treats a participant
# whose prepare failed as having nothing to undo, and declares the aborted saga
# done once every participant that ACKED has applied the abort. A failed
# prepare is not proof that nothing was staged - a write that timed out after
# staging its bucket also nacks - so those buckets are never told the outcome.
# Every saga still reaches "done", so Termination stays green, and only aborted
# sagas are affected, so EveryCommittedKeyReadable stays green too. Of the
# three liveness properties only NoStrandedPrepare sees it (issue #2321).
MODULE: NoStrandedPrepareCompensationSkipsNacked
TARGET: NoStrandedPrepare
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the compensation fan-out skips participants whose prepare failed, so their staged buckets are never told the abort
PERTURBS: BroadcastStep

--- FIND
           allDone == \A j \in Written(t) : nterm[j] # "none"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: during compensation a nacked participant counts as done whether
\* or not it has applied the abort terminal.
           allDone == \A j \in Written(t) :
                        nterm[j] # "none" \/ (phase[t] = "aborting" /\ vote[t][j] = "nack")
--- END